§ `s 7 -- consumer, trader, consumer/trader claim`

-- c070: Chloe and the retailer.
#ASSERT `Am I a consumer` `Chloe's laptop refund claim`
#ASSERT NOT `Am I a consumer` `a laptop bought for my business, replacement sought`

#ASSERT `Is the other party a trader` `Chloe's laptop refund claim`
#ASSERT NOT `Is the other party a trader` `a fee dispute with a professional outside trade or commerce`

#ASSERT `Is my claim a consumer/trader claim` `Chloe's laptop refund claim`
#ASSERT NOT `Is my claim a consumer/trader claim` `an $80,000 claim against a trader`

§ `ss 6, 10 -- can the Court hear my claim`

#ASSERT `Can the Magistrates Court hear my claim` `Chloe's laptop refund claim` EQUALS `yes, as a consumer/trader claim`
#ASSERT `Can the Magistrates Court hear my claim` `a laptop bought for my business, replacement sought` EQUALS `no: only a consumer/trader claim can seek work, services, return or replacement`
#ASSERT `Can the Magistrates Court hear my claim` `a $75,000 debt` EQUALS `yes, within the general civil jurisdiction`
#ASSERT `Can the Magistrates Court hear my claim` `an $80,000 debt` EQUALS `no: it is more than the jurisdictional limit`
#ASSERT `Can the Magistrates Court hear my claim` `an $80,000 debt, the debtor consenting` EQUALS `yes, because the other party consents`
#ASSERT `Can the Magistrates Court hear my claim` `a $5,000 defamation claim, the other party consenting` EQUALS `no: the Court has no jurisdiction over a claim of that kind (s 6(5))`

§ `s 26 -- minor case`

-- c070: Chloe can bring her laptop claim as a minor case.
#ASSERT `Can I bring my claim as a minor case` `Chloe's laptop refund claim`
#ASSERT `Can I bring my claim as a minor case` `a $10,000 claim, elected`
#ASSERT NOT `Can I bring my claim as a minor case` `a $10,001 claim, elected`

#ASSERT `Is my claim a minor case` `Chloe's laptop refund claim`
#ASSERT NOT `Is my claim a minor case` `Chloe's laptop refund claim, not elected`
#ASSERT `Is my claim a minor case` `a $12,000 claim against a trader, the parties agreeing on a minor case`

§ `ss 27, 28 -- procedure`

#ASSERT `Which procedure will my case follow` `Chloe's laptop refund claim` EQUALS `the minor cases procedure`
#ASSERT `Which procedure will my case follow` `a $12,000 claim against a builder of a deck` EQUALS `the general procedure: it is not a minor case`
#ASSERT `Which procedure will my case follow` `a $5,000 claim under Commonwealth law, elected` EQUALS `the general procedure: the Court must order it for Commonwealth jurisdiction (s 28(2))`
#ASSERT `Which procedure will my case follow` `a $5,000 claim with complex facts, elected` EQUALS `the minor cases procedure, unless the Court orders the general procedure (s 28(3))`

#ASSERT `Will the Court first try to settle my case` `Chloe's laptop refund claim`

§ `ss 29, 45 -- the hearing`

#ASSERT `Will my hearing be in private` `Chloe's laptop refund claim` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Will my hearing be in private` `a $75,000 debt` FALSE

#ASSERT NOT `Is the Court bound by the rules of evidence` `Chloe's laptop refund claim`

§ `ss 30, 44 -- representation`

-- c070: Chloe's laptop claim is a consumer/trader claim, so s 30(5) and not s 30(4) governs a lawyer.
#ASSERT NOT `May a lawyer represent me` `Chloe's laptop refund claim` `no agreement and no leave`
#ASSERT `May a lawyer represent me` `Chloe's laptop refund claim` `all parties agreeing`
#ASSERT `May a lawyer represent me` `Chloe's laptop refund claim` `the Court satisfied no one is disadvantaged`
#ASSERT NOT `May a lawyer represent me` `Chloe's laptop refund claim` `the Court satisfied only of the interests of justice`

#ASSERT `May a non-lawyer represent me` `Chloe's laptop refund claim` `the Court seeing an unfair disadvantage at trial`
#ASSERT NOT `May a non-lawyer represent me` `a $75,000 debt` `the Court seeing an unfair disadvantage at trial`
#ASSERT `May a non-lawyer represent me` `a $75,000 debt` `exceptional circumstances found`

§ `ss 25, 31 -- costs`

#ASSERT `What costs can the winner recover` `Chloe's laptop refund claim` `no special costs findings` EQUALS `only the allowable costs: court fees, service fees and enforcement costs (s 31(2))`
#ASSERT `What costs can the winner recover` `Chloe's laptop refund claim` `a claim wholly without merit` EQUALS `the allowable costs and the other costs, the Court being satisfied under s 31(3)`
#ASSERT `What costs can the winner recover` `an $8,000 loan to a friend, not elected` `no special costs findings` EQUALS `only the allowable costs: court fees, service fees and enforcement costs (s 31(2))`
#ASSERT `What costs can the winner recover` `a $12,000 claim against a builder of a deck` `no special costs findings` EQUALS `the whole of the winner's costs, unless the Court finds good reason not to (s 25(2))`
#ASSERT `What costs can the winner recover` `a $12,000 claim against a trader, the parties agreeing on a minor case` `no special costs findings` EQUALS `only the allowable costs: court fees, service fees and enforcement costs (s 31(2))`

#ASSERT NOT `Could I have to pay the other side's legal fees if I lose` `Chloe's laptop refund claim` `no special costs findings`
#ASSERT `Could I have to pay the other side's legal fees if I lose` `a $12,000 claim against a builder of a deck` `no special costs findings`

§ `ss 32, 40 -- appeals`

#ASSERT `Can I appeal and to whom` `Chloe's laptop refund claim` `the judgment` `a magistrate` `the Court got the facts or the law wrong` EQUALS `no appeal lies (s 32)`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal and to whom` `Chloe's laptop refund claim` `the judgment` `a magistrate` `I was denied natural justice` EQUALS `to the District Court under Part 7 (ss 32(2)(a), 40)`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal and to whom` `Chloe's laptop refund claim` `the judgment` `a registrar or other non-magistrate` `I was denied natural justice` EQUALS `to a magistrate, under the rules of court (s 32(2)(b))`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal and to whom` `a $12,000 claim against a builder of a deck` `the judgment` `a magistrate` `the Court got the facts or the law wrong` EQUALS `to the District Court (s 40(1))`

#ASSERT `How many days do I have to appeal` `Chloe's laptop refund claim` `the judgment` `a magistrate` `I was denied natural justice` EQUALS JUST 21

